# ── API ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave both unset during development. `src/lib/env.ts` then derives the host
# from the machine already serving the JS bundle, which is by definition
# reachable from the device — that is how the app got there.
#
# Set them when the API is not on the dev machine, or for any release build
# (which has no dev server to infer a host from).
#
# `localhost` is never right here. To a phone, localhost is the phone.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.50:3002/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=http://192.168.1.50:3002

# Production
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.zassdeliver.com/api/v1
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SOCKET_URL=https://api.zassdeliver.com

# ── Native build secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
# Read by app.config.ts at build time. Never committed; on EAS these live in
# `eas env` / EAS secrets rather than in this file.

# Android needs a Google Maps key for the live tracking map. Without one the
# order screen shows a map-less route card instead (a MapView with no key
# crashes the app, so it is never mounted). Enable "Maps SDK for Android".
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_KEY=

# Printed by `eas init`. Not a secret. The update URL is derived from it
# (https://u.expo.dev/<id>), so EXPO_UPDATE_URL is only needed to override.
#
# This file is gitignored, so EAS cloud builds never see it. Mirror these
# into each environment with `eas env:create --environment <profile> ...`.
EAS_PROJECT_ID=
# EXPO_UPDATE_URL=
